---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Data Sourcing Policy | LeadVault"
  description="How LeadVault sources, verifies, and handles the business contact data in the datasets we sell — and how to request removal."
  path="/data-sourcing-policy"
  heading="Data Sourcing Policy"
  lastUpdated="August 15, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how LeadVault sources and handles the business contact data that appears
    in the datasets we deliver to clients — separate from
    <a href="/privacy-policy">our Privacy Policy</a>, which covers information from visitors to
    this website and people who submit our forms.
  </p>

  <h2>What We Source</h2>
  <p>
    LeadVault provides <strong>business contact data only</strong> — names, job titles, company
    names, business email addresses, business phone numbers (where available), locations, and
    industries of professionals and companies relevant to a client's specification. We do not
    collect or sell sensitive personal information: no government ID numbers, financial account
    details, health information, or similarly sensitive categories of personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Where It Comes From</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Publicly available information</strong> — business listings, professional profiles, company websites, and other public sources.</li>
    <li><strong>Licensed partners</strong> — data providers we've vetted and contracted with.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct research</strong> — our team and tools compiling records to a client's specific request.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Verification Before Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Every record passes through our in-house verification pipeline before it reaches a client:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email verification — MX record checks across all major provider types (Office 365, Google Workspace, and others), confirming the address is real and deliverable.</li>
    <li>Bounce &amp; hygiene screening — dormant mailboxes and dead domains are filtered out before delivery.</li>
    <li>Duplicate removal and basic data-quality checks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Compliance Alignment</h2>
  <p>
    Our sourcing and handling practices are built around: public business data only, no sensitive
    personal information, alignment with the principles of the Nigeria Data Protection Act and the
    EU GDPR (including a legitimate-interest basis for B2B contact data), honoring removal requests
    promptly, and compliance with CAN-SPAM and applicable anti-spam law for any campaign we run on
    a client's behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>Order Screening</h2>
  <p>
    We review incoming orders and decline any request we reasonably believe is intended for
    fraudulent, deceptive, or harassing purposes, or that targets individuals or categories of data
    outside the scope described above.
  </p>

  <h2>If You're an Individual Whose Business Contact Information Appears in Our Data</h2>
  <p>
    If you'd like a record about you removed from our sourcing pipeline and any dataset we hold, or
    have questions about how your business contact information was sourced, submit a request on our
    <a href="/removal-request">Removal Request</a> page. We process removal requests promptly and
    will not knowingly re-source a record you've asked us to remove.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    Datasets are protected with encryption, access controls, and secure delivery methods from the
    point of sourcing through delivery to a client.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy as our sourcing practices or the law changes. The "Last updated" date
    above reflects the most recent revision.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about how we source data? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
